{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A distortionless channel has K = 3 and td = 2 ms. The input is 2 cos(500t) V. Find the output.",say:'Question two. A distortionless channel: gain three, delay two milliseconds, input two cosine five hundred t volts. Find the output.',cues:{k:'Question two',q:'A distortionless channel'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A distortionless channel has K = 3 and td = 2 ms. The input is 2 cos(500t) V. Find the output.",say:'The input is in the band. Amplitude: three times two, six volts. The phase is minus five hundred times two milliseconds, minus one radian. So y is six cosine of five hundred t minus one.',cues:{fk:'The input is',k1:'in the band',k2:'Amplitude: three',k3:'The phase is minus',k3b:'minus one radian',k4:'So y is six'},calc:{f:['|H| = K,  ∠H = −ω'+HT_td],hint:'Read ω from the input: 500 rad/s.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Band","ω = 500 rad/s, inside the band","k1"],["Amplitude","3 × 2 V = 6 V","k2"],["Phase",["∠H = −(500)(2 × 10⁻³)","∠H = −1 rad"],["k3","k3b"]],["Output","y(t) = 6 cos(500t − 1) V","k4"]],live:[0,1,2,3]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"An ideal low-pass filter with td = 0 is shifted to td = 5 ms. Is the shifted filter causal? Explain.",say:'Question three. An ideal low-pass filter is shifted to a five millisecond delay. Is it causal? Explain.',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'An ideal low-pass'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"An ideal low-pass filter with td = 0 is shifted to td = 5 ms. Is the shifted filter causal? Explain.",say:`No, it is not. The shifted ${P('sinc')} is still nonzero at infinitely many times before the delay, back to minus infinity, even between zero and five milliseconds. No finite shift removes that left tail.`,cues:{a1:'No, it is not',a2:'The shifted',a3:'No finite shift'},al:[["No.",'a1'],["The shifted response sin(ωc(t − td))/(π(t − td)) is nonzero for infinitely many t < td, back to −∞, including some in 0 < t < td.",'a2'],["Any finite shift leaves an infinite left tail: only td → ∞ would make it causal.",'a3']],vis:(c,u,b)=>`
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),HT_L(20,300,600,300,HT_GRY,2)+HT_L(213.3,80,213.3,330,INK,3)+HT_T(213.3,362,'t = 0',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle'})+HT_T(600,336,'t',{fs:24,a:'end',fill:HT_MUT}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),HT_curve(t=>HT_sinc(Math.PI*(t-5)),-6,12,20,600,300,180,BLU,4,360)+HT_L(374.4,110,374.4,330,BLU,2,HT_dash)+HT_T(374.4,362,HT_sb('t','d')+' = 5 ms',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a3'),`<rect x="20" y="200" width="193.3" height="140" fill="${RED}" fill-opacity=".12"/>`+HT_arrow(200,420,30,420,RED,4)+HT_T(116,456,'… to −∞',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:RED})+HT_T(380,456,'nonzero before t = 0',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:RED}))}`},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:`Your free notes are the PDF in the description. Redraw the ideal filter, the autocorrelation pair and the ${P('Hilbert')} pair.`,cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the ideal'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["The three chapters", "Distortionless transmission and ideal filters; correlation and spectral density; the Hilbert transform"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["The ideal filter", "Gain 2 inside |ω| ≤ 2000 rad/s, zero outside, and a straight phase line; cos 1000t comes out twice as tall and 1 ms later."], ["The autocorrelation pair", "Rₓ(τ) of e⁻²ᵗu(t) is even with its peak 0.25 at τ = 0; its Fourier transform is 1/(4 + ω²) = |X(ω)|²."], ["The Hilbert pair", "cos 2t becomes sin 2t, a quarter period later: phase −90° for ω > 0 and +90° for ω < 0, gain 1."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: Alan V. Oppenheim and Alan S. Willsky (Signals and Systems); B. P. Lathi and Roger A. Green (Linear Systems and Signals); Simon Haykin and Barry Van Veen (Signals and Systems)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:`So remember: flat gain and straight phase keep the shape, correlation finds the match, and ${P('Hilbert')} turns every phase ninety degrees. Next time, ${P('Laplace')} transform analysis. See you there!`,cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'flat gain and',w2:'correlation finds',w3:'turns every phase',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['FLAT GAIN + STRAIGHT PHASE','BLU','w1'],['CORRELATION FINDS THE MATCH','ORG','w2'],['A 90° TURN, GAIN 1','GRN','w3']],next:["UP NEXT", "Next topic", "Laplace Transform Analysis", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
